<h2>Who we are</h2>
<p>HelioLattice provides ERP and CRM software for rooftop solar installers and EPC companies in India. You can contact us at <a href="mailto:support@heliolattice.com">support@heliolattice.com</a> about anything in this policy.</p>

<h2>Information we collect</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Information you give us.</strong> When you request a demo or write to us, you may share your name, company, city, role, work email, phone number and details about your business.</li>
  <li><strong>Usage information.</strong> We use Microsoft Clarity to understand how visitors use this website. Clarity collects information such as pages viewed, clicks, scrolling, device and browser type, approximate location and session recordings. Clarity masks sensitive input fields, and you should avoid typing personal data anywhere other than our contact and demo forms.</li>
  <li><strong>Technical information.</strong> Our hosting provider processes standard request data, such as IP address and browser details, to deliver and protect the site.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
<p>Microsoft Clarity sets cookies and similar identifiers so it can recognise a visit across pages. You can block or delete cookies through your browser settings, and the site continues to work. If we add other analytics, such as Google Analytics, we will update this policy.</p>

<h2>How we use information</h2>
<ul>
  <li>To reply to your messages and arrange demos.</li>
  <li>To prepare quotes and proposals you ask for.</li>
  <li>To understand how the website is used and improve its content and design.</li>
  <li>To keep the website secure and to meet legal obligations.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Who we share information with</h2>
<p>We share information with service providers who help us run the website and handle enquiries, such as hosting, analytics (Microsoft Clarity) and form or email providers. They process it for the purpose of providing their service. We share information with authorities where the law requires it. Personal information is never sold.</p>

<h2>How long we keep information</h2>
<p>We keep enquiry details for as long as needed to respond and to manage any resulting relationship, and for a reasonable period afterwards for our records. Analytics data is kept according to the retention settings of the analytics provider.</p>

<h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
<p>You may ask us to access, correct or delete personal information you have given us, or withdraw consent to our use of it, subject to applicable law including India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023. Write to <a href="mailto:support@heliolattice.com">support@heliolattice.com</a> and we will respond.</p>

<h2>Customer data in the software</h2>
<p>Data that customers enter into HelioLattice, such as their own enquiries, projects and documents, belongs to the customer and is handled under the agreement we sign with them.</p>

<h2>Security</h2>
<p>We use reasonable measures to protect information. You can read about the controls in the software on our <a href="/security/">security page</a>.</p>

<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>We may update this policy and will change the date above when we do.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>For privacy questions, write to <a href="mailto:support@heliolattice.com">support@heliolattice.com</a>.</p>
